    "habitat": "continental_slope",
    "order": 72,
    "notes": "Brittle star of the soft-bottom slope carpets off northern Japan: a flat, round central disc about 2.5 cm across (notched where each arm joins, with small arm combs) and five long, thin, jointed, snake-like arms 3-4 times the disc diameter; reddish brown to brick above, paler below. Crawls by rowing its arms. No bioluminescence recorded for this species.",
